# Creating the FastText Refusal Model

## Step 1: Download the Dataset

Download the dataset from Kaggle:

https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/karimmahmoud09/llm-refusal-responses-dataset

## Step 2: Add the Dataset

Place the downloaded dataset in the following directory:

```text
evaluation/
└── refusal/
    └── data/
```

## Step 3: Download the FastText Embedding Model

Download the pre-trained FastText word vectors from:

https://fasttext.cc/docs/en/crawl-vectors.html

Place the downloaded embedding file in:

```text
evaluation/
└── refusal/
    └── models/
```

## Step 4: Train the Model

Run the training script located in the `src` directory.


# Running the Refusal dynamic embedding Classifier on Kaggle

## Step 1: Create a Notebook

* Go to **Kaggle**.
* Select **Create → New Notebook**.
* Click **File → Import Notebook**.
* Upload:

  ```
  refusal-model-dl-bert.ipynb
  ```

## Step 2: Enable GPU

* Open the **Session options** panel on the right.
* Set **Accelerator** to:

  ```
  GPU T4 x2
  ```
* Click **Save**.

## Step 3: Add the Dataset

* Click **Add Data**.
* Search for:

  use:

  ```
  https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/mariamamin30/refusal-llm
  ```
* Add the dataset to the notebook.

The dataset will be available at:

```text
/kaggle/input/refusal-llm/
```

## Step 4: Train the Model

Click **Run All** to execute all notebook cells.


## Step 5: Copy the Model

Place the downloaded model at:

```text
evaluation/
└── refusal/
    └── models/
        └── lstm_refusal_model_bert.pt
```

---


# Creating the FastText PII Model

## Step 1: Download the Dataset

Download the dataset from Kaggle:

https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/karimmahmoud09/pii-splited-data?select=train.parquet

## Step 2: Add the Dataset

Place the downloaded dataset in the following directory:

```text
defender/
└── pii_detection/
    └── data/
```

## Step 3: Download the FastText Embedding Model

Download the pre-trained FastText word vectors from:

https://fasttext.cc/docs/en/crawl-vectors.html

Place the downloaded embedding file in:

```text
defender/
└── pii_detection/
    └── models/
```

## Step 4: Train the Model

Run the `fasttext_pii` training script located in the `train` directory.

---

# Running the PII Detection dynamic embedding Model on Kaggle

## Step 1: Create a Notebook

* Go to **Kaggle**.
* Select **Create → New Notebook**.
* Click **File → Import Notebook**.
* Upload:

  ```
  pii-bilstm-context-bert-bilstm-crf.ipynb
  ```

## Step 2: Enable GPU

* Open the **Session options** panel.
* Set **Accelerator** to:

  ```
  GPU T4 x2
  ```
* Click **Save**.

## Step 3: Add the Dataset

* Click **Add Data**.
* Search for:

   use:

  ```
  https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/karimmahmoud09/pii-safety-dataset
  ```
* Add the dataset.

The dataset will be available at:

```text
/kaggle/input/pii-safety-dataset/
```

## Step 4: Train the Model

Click **Run All** to execute all notebook cells.

## Step 5: Copy the Model

Place the downloaded model at:

```text
defenders/
└── pii_detection/
    └── models/
        └── distilbert_bilstm_crf.pt
```

---

# Creating the Dialogue Dynamics Model

## Step 1: Download the Dataset

Download the dataset from Kaggle:

https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/karimmahmoud09/dialogue-dynamics-dataset

## Step 2: Add the Dataset

Place the downloaded dataset in the following directory:

```text
defender/
└── multi_turn/
    └── NBF/
        └── data/
```

## Step 3: Train the Model

Run the training script.

## Step 4: Move the Trained Model

After training is complete, move the generated model file to the following directory:

```text
defender/
└── multi_turn/
    └── integrated/
        └── models/
```